{"id":"1d4b6ca7576027a1","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-symmetric-model-construction.md","title":"Symmetric Model Construction","display":"thm-symmetric-model-construction — Symmetric Model Construction","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-symmetric-model-construction","aliases":["58-thm-symmetric-model-construction","Symmetric Model Construction","Symmetric Submodel"],"display":"thm-symmetric-model-construction — Symmetric Model Construction","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-generic-extension.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-generic.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-name-evaluation.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-name.md]]","[[58-df-bijective]]","[[../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-poset.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-symmetric-model-construction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-symmetric-model-construction</span><span>Symmetric Model Construction</span><span>Symmetric Submodel</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-symmetric-model-construction — Symmetric Model Construction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"76dde059f166d3e6\" href=\"?note=76dde059f166d3e6\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-generic-extension.md\">../batch13/58-df-generic-extension.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"545853811ce0a4b6\" href=\"?note=545853811ce0a4b6\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-generic.md\">../batch16/58-df-generic.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md\">../batch06/58-df-ctm.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0c40d420e5118724\" href=\"?note=0c40d420e5118724\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-name-evaluation.md\">../batch05/58-df-name-evaluation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-name.md\">../batch07/58-df-name.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"58-df-bijective\">58-df-bijective</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"59685d062adf2748\" href=\"?note=59685d062adf2748\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md\">../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-poset.md\">../batch02/58-df-poset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F,G,E,N\\in V\">\\(M,P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F,G,E,N\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)\">\\(\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)\">\\(\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)\\)</span> are the imported exact model, genericity, and extension predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}\\)</span> are the imported typed predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\">\\(\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S\\)</span> are the local notions defined below</li>\n<li>The action of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\\in\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\">\\(\\pi\\in\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-names is lifted recursively by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi\\cdot\\tau=\\{\\langle\\pi\\cdot\\sigma,\\pi(p)\\rangle:\\langle\\sigma,p\\rangle\\in\\tau\\}\">\\(\\pi\\cdot\\tau=\\{\\langle\\pi\\cdot\\sigma,\\pi(p)\\rangle:\\langle\\sigma,p\\rangle\\in\\tau\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)\">\\(\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)\\)</span> is the least set of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-names containing <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau\">\\(\\tau\\)</span> and every name occurring recursively in it</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)\">\\(\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)\\)</span> are the imported name and four-place name-evaluation predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\)</span> is the imported set-ordinal predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\">\\(\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\)</span> is the set of hereditarily <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F\">\\(\\mathcal F\\)</span>-symmetric names defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}automorphisms\\text{-}for\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}models}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\\coloneqq\\{\\pi\\in\\mathcal P(P\\times P):{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,P,P)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall p,q\\in P\\;\\bigl(\n\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in R\n\\leftrightarrow\\langle\\pi(p),\\pi(q)\\rangle\\in R\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}automorphisms\\text{-}for\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}models}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\\coloneqq\\{\\pi\\in\\mathcal P(P\\times P):{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,P,P)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall p,q\\in P\\;\\bigl(\n\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in R\n\\leftrightarrow\\langle\\pi(p),\\pi(q)\\rangle\\in R\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}subgroup\\text{-}filter}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathcal F\\subseteq\\{H\\subseteq\\Gamma:\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\}\n\\land\\Gamma\\in\\mathcal F\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H,K\\in\\mathcal F\\;(H\\cap K\\in\\mathcal F)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall K\\subseteq\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(K,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\land H\\subseteq K\\to K\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall\\pi\\in\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\{\\pi\\circ h\\circ\\pi^{-1}:h\\in H\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}subgroup\\text{-}filter}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathcal F\\subseteq\\{H\\subseteq\\Gamma:\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\}\n\\land\\Gamma\\in\\mathcal F\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H,K\\in\\mathcal F\\;(H\\cap K\\in\\mathcal F)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall K\\subseteq\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(K,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\land H\\subseteq K\\to K\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall\\pi\\in\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\{\\pi\\circ h\\circ\\pi^{-1}:h\\in H\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}system}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\n\\land\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(\\Gamma,\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R),\\circ)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}system}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\n\\land\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(\\Gamma,\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R),\\circ)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hereditarily\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}names}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\coloneqq\\{\\tau\\in M:{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Name}(\\tau,P)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\sigma\\in\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)\\;\n\\bigl(\\{\\pi\\in\\Gamma:\\pi\\cdot\\sigma=\\sigma\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hereditarily\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}names}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\coloneqq\\{\\tau\\in M:{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Name}(\\tau,P)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\sigma\\in\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)\\;\n\\bigl(\\{\\pi\\in\\Gamma:\\pi\\cdot\\sigma=\\sigma\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}model\\text{-}construction}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\n\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists E,N\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land N=\\{x\\in V:\\exists\\tau\\in\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\;\n\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{CTM}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land M\\subseteq N\\subseteq E\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\to(\\alpha\\in N\\leftrightarrow\\alpha\\in M)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}model\\text{-}construction}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\n\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists E,N\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land N=\\{x\\in V:\\exists\\tau\\in\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\;\n\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{CTM}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land M\\subseteq N\\subseteq E\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\to(\\alpha\\in N\\leftrightarrow\\alpha\\in M)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Symmetric submodels are evaluations of hereditarily symmetric names; an arbitrary condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{sym}(x)\\in\\mathcal F\">\\(\\mathrm{sym}(x)\\in\\mathcal F\\)</span> on extension elements does not define the model.</li>\n<li>The extension <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span>, order <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span>, name action, stabilizer filter, and four-place evaluation predicate are all explicit.  The last conjunct states equality of the models' ordinals without treating <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ord}\">\\(\\operatorname{Ord}\\)</span> as a set.</li>\n<li>Cohen first used symmetric models; they lie between the ground model and its generic extension and can be tailored to make chosen fragments of Choice fail.</li>\n<li>They are the standard tool for forcing failures of chosen fragments of AC while preserving others.</li>\n<li>Cohen's original independence model is a symmetric submodel in this sense.</li>\n<li>Solovay: refined technique.</li>\n<li>Applications: regularity properties, choice hierarchy.</li>\n<li>Foundation: independence proofs in set theory.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-generic-extension.md","status":"resolved","id":"76dde059f166d3e6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-generic-extension.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-generic.md","status":"resolved","id":"545853811ce0a4b6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-generic.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-name-evaluation.md","status":"resolved","id":"0c40d420e5118724","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-name-evaluation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-name.md","status":"resolved","id":"ec28b62254928d73","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-name.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bijective","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bijective]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md","status":"resolved","id":"59685d062adf2748","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-subgroup.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-poset.md","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-poset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"5582a281f15a33c2","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F,G,E,N\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Bijective}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Poset}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi\\in\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi\\cdot\\tau=\\{\\langle\\pi\\cdot\\sigma,\\pi(p)\\rangle:\\langle\\sigma,p\\rangle\\in\\tau\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Name}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ordinal}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal F","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}automorphisms\\text{-}for\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}models}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R)\\coloneqq\\{\\pi\\in\\mathcal P(P\\times P):{}&\n\\mathrm{Bijective}(\\pi,P,P)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall p,q\\in P\\;\\bigl(\n\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in R\n\\leftrightarrow\\langle\\pi(p),\\pi(q)\\rangle\\in R\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}normal\\text{-}subgroup\\text{-}filter}\\vdash\\\\\n&\\quad\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&\\qquad\\mathcal F\\subseteq\\{H\\subseteq\\Gamma:\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(H,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\}\n\\land\\Gamma\\in\\mathcal F\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H,K\\in\\mathcal F\\;(H\\cap K\\in\\mathcal F)\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall K\\subseteq\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(K,\\Gamma,\\circ)\\land H\\subseteq K\\to K\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr)\\\\\n&\\qquad{}\\land\\forall H\\in\\mathcal F\\;\\forall\\pi\\in\\Gamma\\;\\Bigl(\n\\{\\pi\\circ h\\circ\\pi^{-1}:h\\in H\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}system}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\n\\land\\mathrm{Subgroup}_S(\\Gamma,\\operatorname{Aut}(P,R),\\circ)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{NormalSubgroupFilter}_S(\\mathcal F,\\Gamma).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hereditarily\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}names}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\coloneqq\\{\\tau\\in M:{}&\n\\mathrm{Name}(\\tau,P)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall\\sigma\\in\\operatorname{NTC}_P(\\tau)\\;\n\\bigl(\\{\\pi\\in\\Gamma:\\pi\\cdot\\sigma=\\sigma\\}\\in\\mathcal F\\bigr)\\}.\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}symmetric\\text{-}model\\text{-}construction}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{SymmetricSystem}_S(P,R,\\Gamma,\\mathcal F)\n\\land\\mathrm{Generic}(G,P,R,M)\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\\exists E,N\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{GenericExtensionTheory}_S(E,M,\\mathrm{ZF},P,G)\\\\\n&\\hspace{5em}{}\\land N=\\{x\\in V:\\exists\\tau\\in\\mathrm{HS}_{\\mathcal F}^{M}\\;\n\\mathrm{NameEvaluation}_S(x,\\tau,G,P)\\}\\\\\n&\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{CTM}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF})\n\\land M\\subseteq N\\subseteq E\\\\\n&\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\to(\\alpha\\in N\\leftrightarrow\\alpha\\in M)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{sym}(x)\\in\\mathcal F","display":false},{"tex":"E","display":false},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ord}","display":false}],"bytes":4917,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4456","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-symmetric-model-construction.md|58-thm-symmetric-model-construction]]（batch18）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-273","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-ext